# env.example — secrets template for the Hermes profile (OODA direct to Kali).
# Copy to `.env` in the Hermes profile home.
# Hermes NEVER shows the value of .env to the model (verified in docs: .env = secrets).
#
# NEVER put real secrets in this example file nor commit it with values.

# API key for Hermes' LLM PROVIDER (OpenRouter). Hermes reads the LLM key from THIS variable:
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY (NOT HERMES_LLM_API_KEY). The profile (config.yaml) sets model.default to the
# OpenRouter model and the compose injects OPENROUTER_API_KEY into the process. NO interactive
# `hermes setup`. Placeholder (never the real value in the repo):
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=changeme-openrouter-api-key

# Do NOT declare messaging tokens (Telegram/Discord/...): messaging is not used and is an
# untrusted input vector.
#
# There is no endpoint token: the kali-mcp server does not validate a token; endpoint security is
# the isolation of the internal docker network.
